<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Uesugi clan domain</h1><p class="st-meta">1551 CE – 1600 CE (approx.) · capital Kasugayama</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Echigo domain of Uesugi Kenshin, the warrior lord famed for his rivalry with Takeda Shingen and his devotion to the war god Bishamonten.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagao-clan">Nagao</a> family were deputies of the Uesugi governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/echigo-province">Echigo</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Nagao Kagetora</a>, later Uesugi Kenshin, took over the clan in 1548 and secured the province by about 1551, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kasugayama-castle">Kasugayama</a> castle. In 1561 the fugitive <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kanto</a> deputy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-norimasa">Uesugi Norimasa</a> adopted him, giving him the Uesugi name and office.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Kenshin</a> campaigned almost every year, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanto-region">Kanto</a> against the Later Hojo and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shinano-province">Shinano</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/takeda-shingen">Takeda Shingen</a>, with five battles at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battles-of-kawanakajima">Kawanakajima</a>, and later in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etchu-province">Etchu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noto-province">Noto</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/echigo-province">Echigo</a>'s trade in ramie cloth and gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines funded his wars. He defeated an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oda-clan">Oda</a> army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tedorigawa">Tedorigawa</a> in 1577.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kenshin">Kenshin</a> died in 1578; his adopted son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uesugi-kagekatsu">Uesugi Kagekatsu</a> won the succession war and served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, who moved him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> in 1598. After opposing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> in 1600 his lands were cut to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yonezawa-domain">Yonezawa Domain</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/uesugi-clan-domain.jpg" alt="Uesugi clan domain" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Mukai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_Crest_Uesugi_Sasa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1551 CE – 1600 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kasugayama</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Uesugi Kenshin, Uesugi Kagekatsu</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Middle Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Uesugi clan, Nagao-Uesugi of Echigo</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1576&amp;focus=uesugi-clan-domain" aria-label="Uesugi clan domain on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8186 869 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Uesugi clan domain lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8440 1178h0M8493 1070h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8506 1125h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M8506 1125h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Japan. <a href="/atlas?year=1576&amp;focus=uesugi-clan-domain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
